## Why This Is Asked
Tests production-grade RAG design across multilingual, heterogeneous corpora with multi-tenant isolation and performance constraints at scale.

## Key Concepts
- Hierarchical chunking (document → sections → paragraphs) with size optimization
- Multilingual embeddings and incremental refresh pipelines
- Vector DB partitioning with ACLs per tenant
- Two-stage retrieval with semantic search and cross-encoder reranking
- Freshness management, latency budgets (200-500ms), and comprehensive failover strategies

## Code Example
```javascript
// Implementation sketch for chunking and indexing
function chunkDocument(text, maxBytes = 4000) {
  const chunks = [];
  let current = '';

  // Split by paragraphs and respect semantic boundaries
  const paragraphs = text.split(/\n\s*\n/);

  for (const paragraph of paragraphs) {
    if (current.length + paragraph.length > maxBytes) {
      if (current) chunks.push(current.trim());
      current = paragraph;
    } else {
      current += (current ? '\n\n' : '') + paragraph;
    }
  }

  if (current) chunks.push(current.trim());
  return chunks;
}

// Tenant-aware retrieval
async function retrieveChunks(query, tenantId, limit = 5) {
  const embeddedQuery = await embedQuery(query);
  const results = await vectorStore.search({
    vector: embeddedQuery,
    filter: { tenantId },
    limit: limit * 2 // Get more for reranking
  });

  // Rerank with cross-encoder
  return await rerank(query, results).slice(0, limit);
}
```

## Why This Is Asked
This scenario tests the ability to design concrete evaluation frameworks for multi-source policy reasoning in regulated environments—where accuracy and traceability are legally required.

## Key Concepts
- Multi-source faithfulness: Ensuring the model attributes claims to correct sources
- Per-sentence provenance: Granular citation at the sentence level, not just document-level
- Conflict detection: Identifying contradictory information across internal policies and external regulations

## Code Example
```javascript
function extractCitations(answer, sources) {
  const sentences = answer.split(/[.!?]+/).filter(s => s.trim());
  return sentences.map(sentence => {
    const relevantSources = sources.filter(s => 
      sentence.toLowerCase().includes(s.keyphrase.toLowerCase())
    );
    return { sentence: sentence.trim(), citations: relevantSources };
  });
}

function detectConflicts(sources) {
  const conflicts = [];
  for (let i = 0; i < sources.length; i++) {
    for (let j = i + 1; j < sources.length; j++) {
      if (sources[i].contradicts?.(sources[j])) {
        conflicts.push({ sourceA: sources[i], sourceB: sources[j] });
      }
    }
  }
  return conflicts;
}

function generateAnswerWithCitations(query, policyDB, regulatoryDB) {
  const policyResults = policyDB.retrieve(query);
  const regulatoryResults = regulatoryDB.retrieve(query);
  const allSources = [...policyResults, ...regulatoryResults];

  const answer = generateAnswer(query, allSources);
  const citations = extractCitations(answer, allSources);
  const conflicts = detectConflicts(allSources);

  return { answer, citations, conflicts: conflicts.length > 0 ? conflicts : null };
}
```

## Why This Is Asked
Assesses ability to architect a scalable cross-lingual RAG pipeline handling chunking, multilingual embeddings, and vector stores with versioning and TTL. It also probes cross-language retrieval strategies and evaluation plans to reduce hallucinations.

## Key Concepts
- Multilingual embeddings (LaBSE, mBERT) and language tagging
- Document-type aware chunking strategies
- Vector DB indexing with versioning, TTL/decay, and provenance
- Cross-language retrieval + fallback translation
- Evaluation: latency, recall across languages, hallucination rate

## Code Example
```javascript
// Pseudo: bilingual embedder + cross-language retrieve
const embedder = new LaBSEEmbedder({ model: 'labse' })
const index = new VectorDB({ name: 'docs', ... })
async function ingest(doc){
  const chunks = chunkDoc(doc, typeRules[doc.type])
  for (const c of chunks){
    index.upsert({ id: c.id, vec: embedder.embed(c.text), meta: { lang: c.lang, version: doc.version, ts: doc.ts }})
  }
}
async function query(q, lang){
  const v = embedder.embed(q)
  const hits = index.query(v, { k: 5, lang })
  // cross-language re-rank can involve translating top hits or language-agnostic scoring
  return hits
}
```

